# Mako Desktop & Local Agent

Scope: `packages/local-agent/**`, `packages/desktop/**`, local-connection
routing in `app/src/lib/local-agent-client.ts`, `app/src/store/localAgentStore.ts`.

## Architecture invariants

- The Local Agent reuses the api driver layer (`api/src/databases/**`,
  `api/src/services/database-connection.service.ts`) via relative imports.
  Never fork/copy driver logic into the agent — extract shared helpers into
  `api/src/databases/**` or `api/src/services/**` instead (see
  `api/src/databases/console-template.ts` for the pattern).
- Agent HTTP endpoints must mirror the cloud API request/response envelopes
  (`{ success, data?, error? }`) so frontend stores can route by connection id
  without response-shape branching.
- Local connection ids are prefixed `local_`. Frontend routing decisions go
  through `isLocalConnectionId()` — never string-match elsewhere.
- Local connection credentials live encrypted under `~/.mako/agent/` and must
  NEVER be sent to or stored in Mako Cloud. Cloud save payloads must strip
  `local_` connection ids (see `cloudSafeConnectionId` in consoleStore).
- The agent binds 127.0.0.1 only, with a strict CORS origin allowlist.
  Never bind 0.0.0.0, never wildcard origins.
- The desktop shell loads the remote web app; do not bundle app/ UI into the
  Electron binary. Desktop-only behavior belongs in main.ts/preload.ts.

## Build & release

- Agent standalone bundle: `pnpm --filter @mako/local-agent build`
  (esbuild single file, optional native modules stubbed — keep new
  dependencies pure-JS or add fallback stubs in `build.mjs`).
- Desktop packaging: `pnpm --filter @mako/desktop pack:dir` (smoke) or
  `dist` (installers). The agent bundle ships as `resources/agent/index.js`.
- Releases: bump `packages/desktop/package.json` version in the PR; merge to
  master triggers `.github/workflows/release-desktop.yml`, which creates the
  `desktop-vX.Y.Z` tag + GitHub Release. Keep electron-builder
  `artifactName`s stable — the website's evergreen download links
  (`releases/latest/download/<asset>`) depend on them.
- PR smoke build: `.github/workflows/desktop-ci.yml`.

## Testing checklist for agent/desktop changes

1. `pnpm --filter @mako/local-agent typecheck && pnpm --filter @mako/desktop typecheck`
2. Run the agent (`pnpm agent:dev`) and exercise `/health`, `/test-connection`,
   `/execute` against a local database.
3. Bundle (`pnpm --filter @mako/local-agent build`) and re-run with plain
   `node dist/index.js` — catches esbuild/native-module regressions.
4. `pnpm --filter @mako/desktop pack:dir` and launch
   `release/linux-unpacked/mako` to verify the packaged agent spawn.
